# Where this project's part of the gh-pages branch is, relative to the
# branch root. ernic-docs-deploy.yml publishes the Sphinx site there, and
# .github/actions/ernic-publish-perf the performance record in its perf/.
# Neither writes outside it: ernic-docs-deploy's rsync --delete wipes
# everything else in this directory except perf/, so pointing it at the
# root of a gh-pages branch that other projects share would delete their
# sites.
#
# Empty while the project has a gh-pages branch of its own, so the site is
# the branch root and ernic-docs-deploy also keeps the root .nojekyll.
# Under a shared one, it's this project's directory, and the root belongs
# to the branch's owners.
#
# Changing it moves nothing already published, so copy the performance
# record first: see "Changing PAGES_SUBDIR" in ci/README.md.
#
# Both read it through ci/pages-subdir.sh, which doesn't source this file,
# so keep the line plain PAGES_SUBDIR=value, with no quoting or spaces. The
# value is empty or path components of letters, digits, `-` and `_`, each
# starting with a letter or digit (Jekyll drops a directory starting with
# `_`), joined by `/`, with no slash at either end. The script refuses
# anything else, and a file without exactly one PAGES_SUBDIR line.
PAGES_SUBDIR=
